    "sticky_notes": [
        {
            "id": "welcome",
            "text": "**Welcome to Vivid!** Three drums, three shapes. Each drum directly triggers its own visual element \u2014 nothing is pre-animated. The music IS the animation.",
            "x": -125.67348,
            "y": 10.489796,
            "width": 350.0,
            "height": 100.0,
            "color": 0
        },
        {
            "id": "mapping",
            "text": "**Kick** \u2192 big orange circle\n**Snare** \u2192 white diamond\n**Hi-hat** \u2192 small blue hexagon\n\nEach drum's peak feeds a Smooth (envelope follower), which then drives the shape's scale on both axes \u2014 so the shape pulses outward on every hit and decays smoothly between hits.",
            "x": -107.04496,
            "y": 142.43112,
            "width": 320.0,
            "height": 160.0,
            "color": 1
        },
        {
            "id": "envelope_note",
            "text": "**Why Smooth?** A drum's `peak` port is instantaneous \u2014 it spikes to ~0.5 for a few milliseconds then collapses. Without smoothing, the shape would flash too briefly to see. Smooth holds the peak (rise=5ms) and decays slowly (fall=400ms) so each hit lingers as a visible pulse.",
            "x": 380.0,
            "y": 700.0,
            "width": 340.0,
            "height": 130.0,
            "color": 3
        },
        {
            "id": "try_this",
            "text": "**Try this:** Click the DrumSequencer and toggle steps on/off. Watch how the visuals change instantly. Or change the BPM via the metronome \u2014 or change a Smooth's `fall_time` to make pulses decay faster or slower.",
            "x": -101.84743,
            "y": 326.73105,
            "width": 320.0,
            "height": 100.0,
            "color": 2
        }
    ]
